{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1165125-evocations-for-wood-dragon-s-claws","id":1165125,"title":"Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Dragon-Blooded"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-12-04T13:16:46-08:00","id":1165125,"title":"Evocations for Wood Dragon's Claws?","content":"So, sorcerers who take Wood Dragon's Claws as their control spell can create and master Evocations for them. <br /> <br /> Has anybody made up any to go along with it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T13:47:26-08:00","id":1165130,"title":"","content":"Did a site search and I found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/886214-evocations-for-spells-workshop?p=889463#post889463\">an old one </a>made a year and a half ago. Hope that gives you a good starting place!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T13:48:29-08:00","id":1165131,"title":"","content":"My search-fu is weak. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T14:04:09-08:00","id":1165134,"title":"","content":"Takes a lot of practice. Precision is important, and less is more. <br /> <br /> I also spend a LOT of time reading these forums every day so... I might remember where to look a little better than some...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T14:31:57-08:00","id":1165141,"title":"","content":"That set of claws in Arms is gonna be reskinned some for my characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T05:54:21-08:00","id":1165281,"title":"","content":"I've always advocated taking the Evocations from any other 3 dot artifact weapon and re-fluffing them for taste. Spring Razor's set, for example, is very thematic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T06:33:51-08:00","id":1165286,"title":"","content":"Lots of good ideas, thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T06:40:51-08:00","id":1165288,"title":"","content":"I'd be tempted to have it grow vine-constructs and use the evocations of the Distaff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T07:48:18-08:00","id":1165303,"title":"","content":"remember that evocations are supposed to be individualized. I feel like none would be more unique to the individual than evocations for a spell construct. <br /> <br /> Also remember that they should be approximately at the level of a 3-dot artifact (at least according to the Devs). which means that there's a max of 10-ish, and they should roughly focus on enhancing your abilities in some way. <br /> <br /> If you have any ideas that you want the forum to take a shot at, there's a few really good charm writers around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my homebrew exalt: The Fabulists - Chosen of the Raksha <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1141861-peach-new-exalt-splat-the-fabulist-exalts-chosen-of-the-raksha\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8804-armyofwhispers","name":"armyofwhispers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8804_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"790"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-05T12:01:15-08:00","id":1165380,"title":"","content":"A guy in my group wrote up some Evocations for his Wood Dragon Claw, though I don't have the actual notes. If I remember correct one of his Evocations would let him shove his hand into the ground, at which point it would turn into a vine and could then pop out of the ground elsewhere, letting him make a Melee attack against someone at up to Medium range. He had another one that would let him create a poison (actually he was implanting a seed in their body) - if someone died while poisoned, their body quickly decay as numerous flowers sprung across it.<br /> <br /> For the last Evocation, he could spend extra Essence to create a more powerful poison/seed. In that case if someone died while under it, a massive flower with a fruit (about the size of a basketball) would grow from the corpse. The fruit would break open two rounds later, revealing a small plant creature that was under his character's control - the plant creature would possesses the dead individual's lower soul and some of its memories. It would serve the character loyally for a scene. At the end of the scene it would start to root itself in the ground and then wouldn't be able to move anymore. At that point it would be a perfectly normal and mundane tree though with twisted features reminiscent of the deceased creature's.<br /> <br /> I think he had two other Evocations but I can't remember what they were off hand. Those were the ones he used the most often.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-06T19:37:28-08:00","id":1165742,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>armyofwhispers</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1165125-evocations-for-wood-dragon-s-claws?p=1165303#post1165303\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">remember that evocations are supposed to be individualized. I feel like none would be more unique to the individual than evocations for a spell construct.<br /> <br /> Also remember that they should be approximately at the level of a 3-dot artifact (at least according to the Devs). which means that there's a max of 10-ish, and they should roughly focus on enhancing your abilities in some way.<br /> <br /> <b>If you have any ideas that you want the forum to take a shot at, there's a few really good charm writers around</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is all some idea gathering for a possible Chronicle to start next year, so I have a dozen questions for every idea. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> At this point, I'm working on my fourth (recent) spin through character generation, trying on a bunch of build ideas.<br /> <br /> This particular one is an Eclipse caste diplomat or fixer. He's starting with a bit of oratory and all that good stuff. So he can be ready for battle during social scenes, he's got a bit of Unusual Hide. I'm also taking him unarmed so he'll never be defenseless at the bargaining table or making a speech.<br /> <br /> Part of the experiment with this character is to get Sorcery and Martial Arts working together, so he's starting off with a little Tiger (enough for the Form), Wood Dragon's Claws (exactly for this thread), and Invulnerable Skin of Bronze to layer up with the Unusual Hide and a concealed chain shirt. Doing both MArts and Sorcery is a stretch, but it's an interesting effort. Eclipse charm-learning plus a range of Evocations seems like a good way to mix up some effectiveness and some utility, too, but I haven't worked through any advancement crunch yet.<br /> <br /> Since the WDClaws will be his primary weapon, I made that his control spell. And here we are!<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, in this particular case - which is quite tentative - Evocations for WDClaws that improve defense would be good. This character isn't going to be the heavy in the circle, so fighting for stalemate would be quite valid. <br /> <br /> This character also prefers to resolve conflicts, where possible, without undue waste, so subdual options would be valid as well. <br /> <br /> If he's fighting to stalemate, then supporting the rest of the Circle with stunts, bonuses, and effects would be helpful. <br /> <br /> Especially, thoughts on how current Ex3 Storytellers are building up Evocations like these would be helpful!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T04:36:28-08:00","id":1165818,"title":"","content":"Invulnerable Skin of Bronze isn't compatible with Tiger Style. It's considered medium armour and Tiger Style is only compatible with light.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T05:24:29-08:00","id":1165836,"title":"","content":"I'm definitely making a Fruit of the Broken Heart Evocation for ripping foes hearts out with your claws and turning it into supernatural fruit!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T07:43:12-08:00","id":1165869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1165125-evocations-for-wood-dragon-s-claws?p=1165818#post1165818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Invulnerable Skin of Bronze isn't compatible with Tiger Style. It's considered medium armour and Tiger Style is only compatible with light.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, sorry. I misspelled &quot;Fairly Tough Skin of Bronze&quot;, the similar spell that's just like light armor. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> How would you shift things around, then, for this character build?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-07T09:06:09-08:00","id":1165882,"title":"","content":"I suppose you could use a the Key of Mastery hearthstone to count ISoB as a second control spell and get [essence] extra soak when the spell is inactive (which I don't think counts as armour) but that's a lot of extra investment for a couple of bonus points of soak.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T07:46:52-08:00","id":1166096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1165125-evocations-for-wood-dragon-s-claws?p=1165869#post1165869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, sorry. I misspelled &amp;quot;Fairly Tough Skin of Bronze&amp;quot;, the similar spell that's just like light armor. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> How would you shift things around, then, for this character build?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there anything wrong with an evocation that makes your bronze skin like light armor?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T08:11:23-08:00","id":1166100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1165125-evocations-for-wood-dragon-s-claws?p=1166096#post1166096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Is there anything wrong with an evocation that makes your bronze skin like light armor?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Invulnerable Skin of Bronze does not gain evocations as part of its control spell. Perhaps with a sorcerous artifact it could be possible but not from the base spell. Additionally it would be kind of odd to have another spell (WDC) enhance/change a different spell of the same circle imo.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T08:40:13-08:00","id":1166106,"title":"","content":"Probably because if it did everyone would have &quot;doesn't count as armour&quot; for the first one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T10:52:24-08:00","id":1166128,"title":"","content":"I do really like the WDClaws for character reasons, but in terms of build it is a long stretch to get sorcery just for them. It seems a lot better to go straight melee or brawl and get some decent starting armor. Which is a shame - I was liking how the build was going. It was turning into a super broad-base of overlapping interacting powers and weird combinations.<br /> <br /> I agree with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3166_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3166\" data-vbnamecard=\"3166\">Elfive</a> that avoiding MArts limitations on armor shouldn't be a quick low-level Evocation. It seems that modifying major systems would have to be a higher Essence, if they're possible at all. <br /> <br /> There doesn't seem to be a spell that does exactly what I wanted as far as Soak goes. Wisecrack about Reasonably Tough Skin of Bronze or no. <br /> <br /> I might bring Unbreakable Bones of Stone forward to Ex3, but straight Attribute buffs have always struck me as more of a Lunar thing. Plus, if I do bring it forward, it'll tend to bring those Atts up across the board. <br /> <br /> Thanks for all the input! I'm having fun working through the choices.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T14:47:11-08:00","id":1166162,"title":"","content":"One thing to remember is that spells are not designed iba vacuum. For instance, ISB and Incomparable Body Arsenal combine to give you a baseline 17 soak before stamina, 10 hardness along with a host of tools. I am not sure you\u2019d find a spell that does what you want because synergistic effects could spiral things out of control.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T16:05:54-08:00","id":1166186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1165125-evocations-for-wood-dragon-s-claws?p=1166162#post1166162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing to remember is that spells are not designed iba vacuum. For instance, ISB and Incomparable Body Arsenal combine to give you a baseline 17 soak before stamina, 10 hardness along with a host of tools. I am not sure you\u2019d find a spell that does what you want because synergistic effects could spiral things out of control.</div> </div> </div> </div>I never imagined those two as being usable at the same time. Wouldn't they be a bit like wearing medium and heavy armor at the same time?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T16:15:25-08:00","id":1166189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1165125-evocations-for-wood-dragon-s-claws?p=1166186#post1166186\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I never imagined those two as being usable at the same time. Wouldn't they be a bit like wearing medium and heavy armor at the same time?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only part of Invulnerable Skin of Bronze that doesn't stack with armor is the control spell bonus while the spell is in effect. You can wear armor and be invulnerably skinned. And since Uncomparable Body Arsenal is heavy armor, it should stack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1581-tonberrian","name":"tonberrian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"109"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-08T17:52:28-08:00","id":1166209,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tonberrian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/dragon-blooded/1165125-evocations-for-wood-dragon-s-claws?p=1166189#post1166189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only part of Invulnerable Skin of Bronze that doesn't stack with armor is the control spell bonus while the spell is in effect. You can wear armor and be invulnerably skinned. And since Uncomparable Body Arsenal is heavy armor, it should stack.</div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s been asked and answered in the Q&amp;A thread but yes, tonberrian has the right of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-18T09:36:43-08:00","id":1168542,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it, is there any particular reason why you couldn't make an Evocation (for a different artifact) that has a spell as a prerequisite, upgrading that spell in the same way evocations upgrade charms? You could even do so with martial arts, too - a MA built around a specific spell or set of spells could have them as prerequisites.<br /> <br /> (Although a more likely path seems to be having a artifact whose evocations include MA charms as prerequisites - eg. a sword intended to be used with Single Point. An Exalt who is sufficiently dedicated to one artifact might devise an entire MA intended to be used with it, especially an MA intended to be used with a particular warstrider, but those would obviously be vanishingly rare.)<br /> <br /> Of course, the simplest answer if a spell doesn't do what you want is to make a separate spell that does. This is much easier than trying to modify an existing spell via evocations or whatever because then you can revise the entire effect to be balanced with what you're trying to do with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/517-aquillion","name":"Aquillion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar517_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1341"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}